    "limits": [
      "Both constant-offset intervals are compatible with before/after measurements, not a proof of zero drift between them. No conflict widening or averaging.",
      "Mac/router bounds retain 10ms uptime truncation and measured SSH RTT. PVE/Mac bounds use four software API timestamps. Neither is an RF or NIC hardware timestamp.",
      "P records are post-callback host PS notifications. Gate is a host predicate, not measured per-packet PPE/NPU blocking or physical client wake.",
      "Eligible global P interior continuity and target state checks do not cover repeated unchanged notifications or unknown boundary/timing delays.",
      "First certain ACK progress can follow ambiguous records inside the offset range. ACK progress may acknowledge pre-wake transmissions; it does not identify the first successful post-wake air transmission.",
      "PVE veth capture sees both path directions and GSO. ACK gaps cannot isolate forward/reverse/AP/firmware/RF delay; microsecond backsteps are sorted per flow. Overlap with a host predicate does not prove it blocked accelerated traffic.",
      "Packet origin is actual first outbound payload, not iperf measurement start. This is one paced Mac trial, not proof of original Air repair."
